#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Courses and tutorials {#courses-and-tutorials}"
msgstr "Mga kurso at tutorial {#courses-and-tutorials}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recommended learning material for developing quantum teams. Below are brief "
"learning outcomes and intended audiences for each learning asset. Follow the"
" links for more details on each.\n"
msgstr ""
"Inirerekomendang materyal sa pagkatuto para sa pagpapaunlad ng mga quantum "
"team. Sa ibaba ay mga maikling resulta ng pagkatuto at target na audience "
"para sa bawat learning asset. Sundan ang mga link para sa karagdagang "
"detalye sa bawat isa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Quantum business foundations](/learning/courses/quantum-business-foundations):** \n"
"* Audience: Accessible to anyone. Ideal for raising awareness across the broader institution, possibly not necessary for core team.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: Familiarity with quantum computing terminology, the state of the science, and awareness of a few application areas and areas of potential business value.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Quantum business foundations](/learning/courses/quantum-business-foundations):**\n"
"* Audience: Naa-access ng sinuman. Ideal para sa pagpapataas ng kamalayan sa mas malawak na institusyon, posibleng hindi kinakailangan para sa core team.\n"
"* Mga resulta ng pagkatuto: Pamilyaridad sa terminolohiya ng quantum computing, ang estado ng agham, at kamalayan sa ilang lugar ng aplikasyon at mga lugar ng potensyal na halaga sa negosyo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Basics of quantum information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information):**\n"
"* Audience: Those seeking a deep theoretical foundation for quantum computing: students and early career scientists.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: Theoretical foundations of classical and quantum information, ability to describe quantum systems using linear algebra, describe multi-qubit systems and entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Basics of quantum information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information):**\n"
"* Audience: Ang mga naghahanap ng malalim na teoretikal na pundasyon para sa quantum computing: mga estudyante at mga siyentipikong nasa maagang karera.\n"
"* Mga resulta ng pagkatuto: Mga teoretikal na pundasyon ng klasikal at quantum na impormasyon, kakayahang ilarawan ang mga quantum system gamit ang linear algebra, ilarawan ang mga multi-qubit system at entanglement.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Quantum diagonalization algorithms](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms):** \n"
"* Audience: Those with strong quantum and computing backgrounds seeking to understand prominent and promising algorithms.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: Familiarity with algorithms like VQE, SQD, and SKQD, explain how different algorithms' costs scale with variables like problem size and the number of groups of commuting Pauli operators, and how to choose a good approach.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Quantum diagonalization algorithms](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms):**\n"
"* Audience: Ang mga may matibay na quantum at computing background na naghahanap na maunawaan ang mga kilala at promising na algorithm.\n"
"* Mga resulta ng pagkatuto: Pamilyaridad sa mga algorithm tulad ng VQE, SQD, at SKQD, ipaliwanag kung paano nag-scale ang mga gastos ng iba't ibang algorithm sa mga variable tulad ng laki ng problema at bilang ng mga grupo ng mga commuting Pauli operator, at kung paano pumili ng magandang diskarte.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In addition to these self-guided courses, many tutorials on IBM Quantum&reg;"
" Platform showcase the latest algorithms and most powerful methods. "
"Tutorials tend to be shorter assets, showing a streamlined implementation of"
" a method. Here are a few of particular interest.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bukod sa mga self-guided na kursong ito, maraming tutorial sa IBM "
"Quantum&reg; Platform ang nagpapakita ng mga pinakabagong algorithm at "
"pinaka-makapangyarihang pamamaraan. Ang mga tutorial ay karaniwang mas "
"maikling asset, na nagpapakita ng streamlined na implementasyon ng isang "
"pamamaraan. Narito ang ilang partikular na kawili-wili.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[CHSH inequality](/tutorials/chsh-inequality):** \n"
"* Audience: For users fairly new to quantum computing. \n"
"* Learning outcomes: There are quantum correlations that are stronger than classical physics can explain, familiarity running a job using Qiskit.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[CHSH inequality](/tutorials/chsh-inequality):**\n"
"* Audience: Para sa mga gumagamit na medyo bago sa quantum computing.\n"
"* Mga resulta ng pagkatuto: Mayroong mga quantum correlation na mas malakas kaysa sa maaaring ipaliwanag ng klasikal na pisika, pamilyaridad sa pagpapatakbo ng isang job gamit ang Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Sample-based quantum diagonalization of a chemistry Hamiltonian](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization):** \n"
"* Audience: Those with strong quantum and computing backgrounds seeking to understand prominent and promising algorithms.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: How to use an SQD approach to find the ground state energy of a chemical system.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Sample-based quantum diagonalization of a chemistry Hamiltonian](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization):**\n"
"* Audience: Ang mga may matibay na quantum at computing background na naghahanap na maunawaan ang mga kilala at promising na algorithm.\n"
"* Mga resulta ng pagkatuto: Kung paano gamitin ang isang SQD approach para mahanap ang ground state energy ng isang chemical system.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**[Sample-based Krylov quantum diagonalization of a fermionic lattice model](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization):** \n"
"* Audience: Those with strong quantum and computing backgrounds seeking to understand prominent and promising algorithms.\n"
"* Learning outcomes: Use the Krylov method from linear algebra, combine the speed of SQD with convergence guarantees from the Krylov method, know the conditions for convergence guarantees.\n"
msgstr ""
"**[Sample-based Krylov quantum diagonalization of a fermionic lattice model](/tutorials/sample-based-krylov-quantum-diagonalization):**\n"
"* Audience: Ang mga may matibay na quantum at computing background na naghahanap na maunawaan ang mga kilala at promising na algorithm.\n"
"* Mga resulta ng pagkatuto: Gamitin ang Krylov method mula sa linear algebra, pagsamahin ang bilis ng SQD na may mga garantiya ng convergence mula sa Krylov method, alamin ang mga kondisyon para sa mga garantiya ng convergence.\n"

